# Dependency Review Expectations\n   153\t\n   154\tYalla pulls only what it nee
ds. When you add or update a third-party\n   155\tGo module, follow the checklis
t in\n   156\t[`CONTRIBUTING.md`](./CONTRIBUTING.md#dependency-review-checklist)
and\n   157\texpect the dependency-review CI job to gate the PR. New modules wit
h\n   158\tunknown licenses or known high-severity advisories will be rejected\n
  159\tautomatically.\n   160\t\n   161\t## Container Image Hardening\n   162\t\
n   163\tThe production `Dockerfile` ships the `yalla-api` binary and\n   164\t`
Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla-worker` binary inside a\n   165\t`gcr.io/dis
troless/static-debian12:nonroot` runtime so a leaked or\n   166\tcompromised ima
ge carries no shell, no package manager, no busybox,\n   167\tand no setuid bina
ries — only the service binary and the system CA\n   168\tbundle. The hardening 
posture is part of the public contract and is\n   169\tpinned by `internal/relea
se/container_hardening_static_test.go`; a\n   170\tregression in any one of the 
following is caught at build time:\n   171\t\n   172\t- **Multi-stage build.** T
he Go toolchain, module cache, and source\n   173\t  tree never reach the runtim
e layer. A single-stage Dockerfile is\n   174\t  rejected.\n   175\t- **Distrole
ss `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime stage\'s base image\n   176\t  is pinned to 
`gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (UID/GID\n   177\t  65532). Debian/U
buntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejected because\n   178\t  they reintroduce a sh
